# Raw vendor announcement HTML, fetched on demand by `npm run claims`.
#
# NOT the evidence: each extracted claim stores the table row it was read from, verbatim, in
# data/vendor_claims.json, and that is what a reader checks against the live post. These are
# just a fetch cache, and they were 3.3 MB across three pages — more than half the tracked
# repo for bytes nothing reads. data/cache/*.json (the ingest source caches) stay tracked,
# because the tests and the offline fallback both depend on them.
